Hi [Client Name],<br><br>
Following up on our call. The TSX fell 0.5% Tuesday, driven mainly by weakness in energy and gold names. Oil fell on continued easing of the Strait of Hormuz situation, and gold fell separately on growing expectations of a Federal Reserve rate hike.<br><br>
Overnight, the picture shifted. Micron, a major US chipmaker, reported much stronger than expected earnings, which has reignited enthusiasm for AI-related stocks globally, including names like Celestica here at home. Meanwhile, this morning''s US inflation data came in hot but roughly as expected, which markets are treating as secondary to the Micron news for now.<br><br>
Your overall plan remains on track. I wanted you to have the context for why different parts of the market moved differently this week.<br><br>
