  '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p><strong>DIY investors holding Canadian energy or gold names who are rattled by two down sessions:</strong> They may be considering an emotional exit without understanding the specific, separable mechanisms behind each sector''s decline.</p>
<p><strong>Tech-curious investors who missed the AI infrastructure theme on the way up:</strong> The Micron-driven rally and its Canadian read-through through names like Celestica offers a timely, concrete entry point for a prospecting conversation.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">There has been a lot happening in Canadian markets over the past two days, energy and gold names falling, then a major chip earnings report overnight that has flipped sentiment for tech stocks. Do you have a few minutes to make sure your portfolio reflects what is actually happening rather than just the headlines?</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>A self-directed investor watching daily headlines about falling energy stocks, falling gold, hot inflation data, and a chip-earnings rally has no easy way to determine which of these stories actually matters for their specific holdings versus which is noise. The risk is either overreacting to a single bad sector day or missing a genuine read-through opportunity, like the Micron-to-Celestica connection, because it requires connecting a US earnings report to a specific Canadian stock.</p>
<p>The advisor''s value is precisely this kind of cross-market connective work, done continuously rather than reactively, so the client''s portfolio responds to genuine signal rather than headline volume.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<p>How concentrated is your current portfolio in Canadian energy or materials names specifically?</p>
<p>Do you have any exposure to Canadian technology or AI infrastructure-adjacent names like Celestica?</p>
<p>When you see a hot inflation print and the market does not sell off, do you have a framework for understanding why?</p>
<p>How do you currently decide which daily market headlines are worth acting on versus which are noise?</p>
</div>
